hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2973","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, and Ishaq ibn Ziyad ibn Yazid al-'Attar, and this is the hadith of Bundar. Narrated to us Abu 'Asim. Narrated to us Rabi'ah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hisn. My grandmother Sarrā’ bint Nabhān, who was a matriarch in the pre-Islamic era, narrated to me, and she said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressed us on the Day of the Heads (yawm al-ru’ūs) and said, “Which land is this?”\nWe said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.”\nHe said, “Is it not the Sacred Precinct (al-Mash‘ar al-Harām)?”\nWe said, “Yes.”\nHe said, “Which day is this?”\nWe said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.”\nHe said, “Is it not the middle of the Days of Tashriq?”\nWe said, “Yes.”\nHe then said, “Indeed, your blood, your wealth, and your honor are forbidden to you just as the sanctity of this day is forbidden to you, in this month, in this land.”\nIshaq added: “So let whoever is present convey it to whoever is absent. O Allah, have I conveyed? O Allah, have I conveyed? O Allah, have I conveyed?”\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
